  <section class="mgdb-hero" aria-labelledby="cmm-title">
    <div class="mgdb-hero-emblem">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 96 96" role="img" aria-label="A pachytene chromosome with a FISH signal on its short arm">
        <rect x="40" y="10" width="16" height="76" rx="8" fill="#c9d6bd" />
        <circle cx="48" cy="48" r="10" fill="#501719" />
        <circle cx="48" cy="27" r="6" fill="#f2a515" />
        <circle cx="48" cy="70" r="6" fill="#2f5e2a" />
      </svg>
      <strong>Community<br />Resource</strong>
      <span>NSF-DBI-0321639</span>
    </div>
    <div class="mgdb-hero-body">
      <h1 id="cmm-title">Cytogenetic Map of Maize project</h1>
      <p class="mgdb-hero-tagline">Nomenclature and methods for placing genetically mapped maize markers on pachytene chromosomes, using sorghum BACs as FISH probes.</p>
      <p class="mgdb-hero-description">The project set out to produce a cytogenetic map of the whole maize genome by fluorescence <i>in situ</i> hybridization. Its three aims were a framework map with core bin markers at 10&ndash;20&nbsp;cM intervals, a detailed map of chromosome 9, and the mapping of centromeric loci as an indirect way of locating the centromeres within the linkage maps. This page is the reference for how its probes are named and how each one was selected, detected and measured.</p>
      <div class="mgdb-hero-actions">
        <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-primary" href="#cmm-nomenclature">How a probe name is read</a>
        <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary" href="#cmm-methods">FISH methods</a>
        <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary" href="/data_center/cytogenetic">Cytogenetics Data Hub</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <nav class="mgdb-section-tabs" aria-label="Sections on this page">
